{"qid": "hotpotqa:4cdf613f05eaa834f5867ee486ec94d47587f09b5a7bb6db", "question": "What is the character of fictional character Claire Fraser in a British-American television drama series developed by Ronald D. Moore ?", "answers": ["Claire is a married World War II nurse"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "\n\nClaire Fraser (Claire Randall/Beauchamp) is the protagonist of **Outlander**, the British–American historical drama developed by Ronald D. Moore[6][7]. In the series she is a married World War II military nurse who, in 1945, is transported back in time to 1743 Scotland, where she falls in love with and marries the Highland warrior Jamie Fraser and becomes embroiled in the Jacobite rising[3][6].", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 105991.5, "error": ""}
