{"qid": "2wikimqa:bdb42f1c30e16bbcdf6f0ab7c1f76765ddaa5817ee5e674b", "question": "Who is Charles Willoughby, 10Th Baron Willoughby Of Parham's paternal grandmother?", "answers": ["Lady Frances Manners"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Based on the retrieved information, Charles Willoughby, 10th Baron Willoughby of Parham, was the \"male heir and descendant from the first creation of the barony that commenced with Sir William Willoughby 1st Baron Willoughby of Parham in 1547\"[6].\n\nAccording to the second creation article, Charles Willoughby (the 2nd Baron) was \"the only son of William Willoughby, 1st Baron Willoughby of Parham, Suffolk, and his first wife, **Elizabeth Heneage**, daughter and heir of Sir Thomas Heneage of Hainton, Lincolnshire, by Katherine Skipwith\"[10].\n\nSince Charles Willoughby, 10th Baron Willoughby of Parham, was a descendant of this line, his paternal grandmother would be **Elizabeth Heneage**, who was the first wife of Sir William Willoughby, 1st Baron Willoughby of Parham.", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 42134.6, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:53f6acc70a61443a93c25c91ca7dc7f8780046d02e28c94a", "question": "Who is the paternal grandmother of King Kang Of Zhou?", "answers": ["Yi Jiang"], "status": "ok", "correct": false, "answer": "Based on the information gathered from the knowledge base, I can trace the paternal lineage of King Kang of Zhou:\n\n1. **King Kang of Zhou** was the son of **King Cheng of Zhou** [4].\n2. **King Cheng of Zhou** was the son of **King Wu of Zhou** (the first king of the Zhou Dynasty) [6].\n3. **King Wu of Zhou's mother** was **Tai Ren** [6].\n\nTherefore, the paternal grandmother of King Kang of Zhou is **Tai Ren** (太任). She was the mother of King Wu of Zhou and the wife of King Wen of Zhou [6].", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 21955.8, "error": ""}
{"qid": "2wikimqa:f73db1873c311b2a38f27a52c5e05b021da0c2fe9590dac3", "question": "Who is Gisela Of Hungary's father-in-law?", "answers": ["Géza"], "status": "ok", "correct": true, "answer": "Gisela of Hungary married King Stephen I of Hungary. According to the retrieved evidence, Stephen I was \"the only son of Grand Prince Géza and his wife, Sarolt\"[9]. Therefore, **Géza** (Grand Prince Géza of Hungary) was Gisela of Hungary's father-in-law.", "tool_calls": ["knowledge_base_search", "knowledge_base_search"], "latency_ms": 34926.7, "error": ""}
